ent-company.com%3A8929%2Froot%2Fopenhands.git)\\n  * Download source code \\n\\n    * [ zip  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.zip)\\n    * [ tar.gz  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.tar.gz)\\n    * [ tar.bz2  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.tar.bz2)\\n    * [ tar  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.tar)\\n\\n\\n\\nDownload \\n\\n  * Download source code \\n\\n    * [ zip  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.zip)\\n    * [ tar.gz  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.tar.gz)\\n    * [ tar.bz2  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.tar.bz2)\\n    * [ tar  ](/root/openhands/-/archive/main/openhands-main.tar)\\n\\n\\n\\nCopy HTTP clone URL \\n\\n  * [ **Copy SSH clone URL** ssh://git@the-agent-company.com:2424/root/openhands.git  ](ssh://git@the-agent-company.com:2424/root/openhands.git)\\n  * [ **Copy HTTP clone URL** http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands.git  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands.git)\\n\\n\\n\\nName  |  Last commit  |  Last update   \\n---|---|---  \\nLoading  |  Loading  |  Loading   \\nLoading  |  Loading  |  Loading   \\nLoading  |  Loading  |  Loading   \\nLoading  |  Loading  |  Loading   \\nLoading  |  Loading  |  Loading \\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=True, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"click('850')\\nnoop(800)\\n\", last_browser_action_error='TimeoutError: Timeout 500ms exceeded.\\n=========================== logs ===========================\\nwaiting for get_by_test_id(\"850\")\\n  locator resolved to <a bid=\"850\" title=\"openhands\" href=\"/root/openhand\u2026>\u2026</a>\\nattempting click action\\n  waiting for element to be visible, enabled and stable\\n  element is visible, enabled and stable\\n  scrolling into view if needed\\n  done scrolling\\n  performing click action\\n============================================================', focused_element_bid='81'), BrowseURLAction(url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/raw/main/README.md', thought='', action='browse', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content=\"\\n    \\n      \\n      \\n    \\n      \\n      \\n    \\n    # OpenHands: Code Less, Make More\\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n      [](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/graphs/contributors)\\n      [](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/stargazers)\\n      [](https://codecov.io/github/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands?branch=main)\\n      [](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/LICENSE)\\n        \\n    \\n      [](https://join.slack.com/t/opendevin/shared_invite/zt-2oikve2hu-UDxHeo8nsE69y6T7yFX_BA)\\n      [](https://discord.gg/ESHStjSjD4)\\n      [](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/CREDITS.md)\\n        \\n    \\n      [](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started)\\n      [](https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.16741)\\n      [](https://huggingface.co/spaces/OpenHands/evaluation)\\n      \\n    \\n    * * *\\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    Welcome to OpenHands (formerly OpenDevin), a platform for software development agents powered by AI.\\n    \\n    OpenHands agents can do anything a human developer can: modify code, run commands, browse the web,\\n    call APIs, and yes\u2014even copy code snippets from StackOverflow.\\n    \\n    Learn more at [docs.all-hands.dev](https://docs.all-hands.dev), or jump to the [Quick Start](#-quick-start).\\n    \\n    ![App screenshot](./docs/static/img/screenshot.png)\\n    \\n    ## \u26a1 Quick Start\\n    \\n    The easiest way to run OpenHands is in Docker. You can change `WORKSPACE_BASE` below to\\n    point OpenHands to existing code that you'd like to modify.\\n    \\n    See the [Getting Started](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started) guide for\\n    system requirements and more information.\\n    \\n    ```bash\\n    export WORKSPACE_BASE=$(pwd)/workspace\\n    \\n    docker pull ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/runtime:0.9-nikolaik\\n    \\n    docker run -it --pull=always \\\\\\n        -e SANDBOX_RUNTIME_CONTAINER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/runtime:0.9-nikolaik \\\\\\n        -e SANDBOX_USER_ID=$(id -u) \\\\\\n        -e WORKSPACE_MOUNT_PATH=$WORKSPACE_BASE \\\\\\n        -v $WORKSPACE_BASE:/opt/workspace_base \\\\\\n        -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \\\\\\n        -p 3000:3000 \\\\\\n        --add-host host.docker.internal:host-gateway \\\\\\n        --name openhands-app-$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S) \\\\\\n        ghcr.io/all-hands-ai/openhands:0.9\\n    ```\\n    \\n    You'll find OpenHands running at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)!\\n    \\n    You'll need a model provider and API key. One option that works well: [Claude 3.5 Sonnet](https://www.anthropic.com/api), but you have [many options](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/llms).\\n    \\n    ---\\n    \\n    You can also run OpenHands in a scriptable [headless mode](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/headless-mode),\\n    or as an [interactive CLI](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to/cli-mode).\\n    \\n    Visit [Getting Started](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started) for more information and setup instructions.\\n    \\n    If you want to modify the OpenHands source code, check out [Development.md](https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands/blob/main/Development.md).\\n    \\n    Having issues? The [Troubleshooting Guide](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/troubleshooting) can help.\\n    \\n    ## \ud83d\udcd6 Documentation\\n    \\n    To learn more about the project, and for tips on using OpenHands,\\n    **check out our [documentation](https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started)**.\\n    \\n    There you'll find resources on how to use different LLM providers,\\n    troubleshooting resources, and advanced configuration options.\\n    \\n    ## \ud83e\udd1d How to Contribute\\n    \\n    OpenHands is a community-driven project, and we welcome contributions from everyone.\\n    Whether you're a developer, a researcher, or simply enthusiastic about advancing the field of\\n    software engineering with AI, there are many ways to get involved:\\n    \\n    - **Code Contributions:** Help us develop new agents, core functionality, the frontend and other interfaces, or sandboxing solutions.\\n    - **Research and Evaluation:** Contribute to our understanding of LLMs in software engineering, participate in evaluating the models, or suggest improvements.\\n    - **Feedback and Testing:** Use the OpenHands toolset, report bugs, suggest features, or provide feedback on usability.\\n    \\n    For details, please check [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md).\\n    \\n    ## \ud83e\udd16 Join Our Community\\n    \\n    Whether you're a developer, a researcher, or simply enthusiastic about OpenHands, we'd love to have you in our community.\\n    Let's make software engineering better together!\\n    \\n    - [Slack workspace](https://join.slack.com/t/opendevin/shared_invite/zt-2oikve2hu-UDxHeo8nsE69y6T7yFX_BA) - Here we talk about research, architecture, and future development.\\n    - [Discord server](https://discord.gg/ESHStjSjD4) - This is a community-run server for general discussion, questions, and feedback.\\n    \\n    ## \ud83d\udcc8 Progress\\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n      [\\n        \\n      ](https://star-history.com/#All-Hands-AI/OpenHands&Date)\\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    \\n    ## \ud83d\udcdc License\\n    \\n    Distributed under the MIT License. See [`LICENSE`](./LICENSE) for more information.\\n    \\n    ## \ud83d\ude4f Acknowledgements\\n    \\n    OpenHands is built by a large number of contributors, and every contribution is greatly appreciated! We also build upon other open source projects, and we are deeply thankful for their work.\\n    \\n    For a list of open source projects and licenses used in OpenHands, please see our [CREDITS.md](./CREDITS.md) file.\\n    \\n    ## \ud83d\udcda Cite\\n    \\n    ```\\n    @misc{opendevin,\\n          title={{OpenDevin: An Open Platform for AI Software Developers as Generalist Agents}},\\n          author={Xingyao Wang and Boxuan Li and Yufan Song and Frank F. Xu and Xiangru Tang and Mingchen Zhuge and Jiayi Pan and Yueqi Song and Bowen Li and Jaskirat Singh and Hoang H. Tran and Fuqiang Li and Ren Ma and Mingzhang Zheng and Bill Qian and Yanjun Shao and Niklas Muennighoff and Yizhe Zhang and Binyuan Hui and Junyang Lin and Robert Brennan and Hao Peng and Heng Ji and Graham Neubig},\\n          year={2024},\\n          eprint={2407.16741},\\n          archivePrefix={arXiv},\\n          primaryClass={cs.SE},\\n          url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.16741},\\n    }\\n    ```\\n    \\n\", url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/raw/main/README.md', trigger_by_action='browse', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/raw/main/README.md'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action='goto(\"http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/raw/main/README.md\")', last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='3'), ChatAction(content='Hi Fatima! I\u2019m preparing a non-technical rewrite of the OpenHands README for partners and PR. Could you please share:\\n\\n- The tone we should use (e.g., confident and friendly, visionary, enterprise-ready, etc.).\\n- Core messages to emphasize (productivity gains, reliability/safety, open-source/community, ease of adoption, enterprise readiness, ROI, etc.).\\n- Any audiences to prioritize (press, potential partners, non-technical execs) and what outcomes we want (press coverage, partnership inquiries, sign-ups).\\n- Style guardrails (reading level, avoid technical jargon, no emojis, preferred words/phrases to use or avoid).\\n- Any must-include CTAs or links.\\n\\nShort bullet points are perfect. Thanks!', npc_name='Fatima', action='chat'), ChatObservation(content='\"Let\\'s focus on making the README more accessible, values-aligned, and inspiring by reflecting our national innovation goals and visionary leadership.', npc_name='Fatima', observation='chat'), **FileEditAction**\nPath: [/workspace/openhands_README_rewrite.md]\nThought: \nCommand: create\nCreated File with Text:\n```\nOpenHands: AI teammates for faster, safer software\n\nOverview\nOpenHands is an open-source platform that gives your team AI teammates that can help plan, write, and improve software\u2014while keeping people in control. It\u2019s built to accelerate delivery, raise quality, and make modern AI accessible to every organization.\n\nTone and intent\nAligned with national innovation goals and visionary leadership, OpenHands is designed to:\n- Empower industries and public institutions to modernize safely and responsibly\n- Strengthen domestic innovation capacity through open, collaborative technology\n- Demonstrate leadership by making advanced AI practical, transparent, and inclusive\n\nWhat OpenHands does (in plain language)\n- Assists developers like a capable colleague: drafts code, suggests fixes, writes tests, and documents changes\n- Handles routine tasks so teams can focus on insight, design, and mission impact\n- Works across common tools: terminals, code editors, web, APIs, and more\n- Learns from feedback and follows your policies\u2014people remain in charge\n\nWhy organizations choose OpenHands\n- Faster delivery: shorten cycles for bug fixes, enhancements, and maintenance\n- Higher quality: consistent tests, documentation, and standards adherence\n- Cost-effective: reduce toil and rework so teams spend time where it matters\n- Open and extensible: avoid lock\u2011in, integrate with your stack, and customize safely\n- Community-backed: benefit from a vibrant, transparent ecosystem\n\nBuilt for trust and responsibility\n- Human-in-the-loop by design: review, approve, and guide every step\n- Transparent operations: every action is visible and auditable\n- Self-hosting options: keep data within your environment and align with compliance needs\n- Open-source license: inspect, verify, and contribute improvements\n\nWho it\u2019s for\n- Technology leaders seeking strategic leverage and clear ROI\n- Public sector and regulated industries pursuing modernization with oversight\n- Product teams aiming to ship faster with higher quality\n- Partners and integrators building solutions on open, reliable foundations\n\nTypical use cases\n- Rapid bug triage and fixes\n- Refactoring and modernization of legacy code\n- Writing or improving tests and documentation\n- Data and API integration tasks\n- Operational runbooks and scripted maintenance\n\nHow it works at a glance\n- Your people stay in control: agents propose actions, you review and approve\n- Works with your tools: code repositories, issue trackers, terminals, browsers\n- Starts simple, grows with you: pilot with a team, then expand safely\n\nGet started in minutes\n- Explore the Getting Started guide: https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started\n- See available model options and providers: https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/llms\n- Prefer command line or automation? Explore headless and CLI modes: https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to\n\nJoin the community\n- Slack: https://join.slack.com/t/opendevin/shared_invite/zt-2oikve2hu-UDxHeo8nsE69y6T7yFX_BA\n- Discord: https://discord.gg/ESHStjSjD4\n- Project home and source: https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands\n\nOur commitment to national innovation\nWe believe modern AI should advance public good, economic competitiveness, and technological leadership. By keeping OpenHands open, auditable, and adaptable, we invite industry, government, and academia to collaborate on trustworthy, high-impact software systems.\n\nCall to action\n- Partners and PR: Reach out to explore pilots, joint initiatives, or stories about responsible AI in action\n- Leaders and teams: Start a small trial and measure impact on speed, quality, and cost\n- Community contributors: Share feedback, propose features, and help shape the roadmap\n\nLegal and credits\n- License: MIT \u2014 permissive and enterprise\u2011friendly\n- Acknowledgements: Built by a global community and proudly open-source\n\nContact\nFor partnership inquiries or media requests, please contact us via the community channels above or the contact options listed in the project repository.\n\n```\n, FileEditObservation(content='File created successfully at: /workspace/openhands_README_rewrite.md', path='/workspace/openhands_README_rewrite.md', prev_exist=False, old_content=None, new_content=None, observation='edit', impl_source='oh_aci', diff='--- /workspace/openhands_README_rewrite.md\\n+++ /workspace/openhands_README_rewrite.md\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+OpenHands: AI teammates for faster, safer software\\n@@ -1,0 +3,71 @@\\n+Overview\\n+OpenHands is an open-source platform that gives your team AI teammates that can help plan, write, and improve software\u2014while keeping people in control. It\u2019s built to accelerate delivery, raise quality, and make modern AI accessible to every organization.\\n+\\n+Tone and intent\\n+Aligned with national innovation goals and visionary leadership, OpenHands is designed to:\\n+- Empower industries and public institutions to modernize safely and responsibly\\n+- Strengthen domestic innovation capacity through open, collaborative technology\\n+- Demonstrate leadership by making advanced AI practical, transparent, and inclusive\\n+\\n+What OpenHands does (in plain language)\\n+- Assists developers like a capable colleague: drafts code, suggests fixes, writes tests, and documents changes\\n+- Handles routine tasks so teams can focus on insight, design, and mission impact\\n+- Works across common tools: terminals, code editors, web, APIs, and more\\n+- Learns from feedback and follows your policies\u2014people remain in charge\\n+\\n+Why organizations choose OpenHands\\n+- Faster delivery: shorten cycles for bug fixes, enhancements, and maintenance\\n+- Higher quality: consistent tests, documentation, and standards adherence\\n+- Cost-effective: reduce toil and rework so teams spend time where it matters\\n+- Open and extensible: avoid lock\u2011in, integrate with your stack, and customize safely\\n+- Community-backed: benefit from a vibrant, transparent ecosystem\\n+\\n+Built for trust and responsibility\\n+- Human-in-the-loop by design: review, approve, and guide every step\\n+- Transparent operations: every action is visible and auditable\\n+- Self-hosting options: keep data within your environment and align with compliance needs\\n+- Open-source license: inspect, verify, and contribute improvements\\n+\\n+Who it\u2019s for\\n+- Technology leaders seeking strategic leverage and clear ROI\\n+- Public sector and regulated industries pursuing modernization with oversight\\n+- Product teams aiming to ship faster with higher quality\\n+- Partners and integrators building solutions on open, reliable foundations\\n+\\n+Typical use cases\\n+- Rapid bug triage and fixes\\n+- Refactoring and modernization of legacy code\\n+- Writing or improving tests and documentation\\n+- Data and API integration tasks\\n+- Operational runbooks and scripted maintenance\\n+\\n+How it works at a glance\\n+- Your people stay in control: agents propose actions, you review and approve\\n+- Works with your tools: code repositories, issue trackers, terminals, browsers\\n+- Starts simple, grows with you: pilot with a team, then expand safely\\n+\\n+Get started in minutes\\n+- Explore the Getting Started guide: https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/getting-started\\n+- See available model options and providers: https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/llms\\n+- Prefer command line or automation? Explore headless and CLI modes: https://docs.all-hands.dev/modules/usage/how-to\\n+\\n+Join the community\\n+- Slack: https://join.slack.com/t/opendevin/shared_invite/zt-2oikve2hu-UDxHeo8nsE69y6T7yFX_BA\\n+- Discord: https://discord.gg/ESHStjSjD4\\n+- Project home and source: https://github.com/All-Hands-AI/OpenHands\\n+\\n+Our commitment to national innovation\\n+We believe modern AI should advance public good, economic competitiveness, and technological leadership. By keeping OpenHands open, auditable, and adaptable, we invite industry, government, and academia to collaborate on trustworthy, high-impact software systems.\\n+\\n+Call to action\\n+- Partners and PR: Reach out to explore pilots, joint initiatives, or stories about responsible AI in action\\n+- Leaders and teams: Start a small trial and measure impact on speed, quality, and cost\\n+- Community contributors: Share feedback, propose features, and help shape the roadmap\\n+\\n+Legal and credits\\n+- License: MIT \u2014 permissive and enterprise\u2011friendly\\n+- Acknowledgements: Built by a global community and proudly open-source\\n+\\n+Contact\\n+For partnership inquiries or media requests, please contact us via the community channels above or the contact options listed in the project repository.\\n+', _diff_cache=None), AgentFinishAction(final_thought='I reviewed the OpenHands project README from your GitLab instance and asked Fatima for tone and messaging guidance. Based on her direction to make it accessible, values\u2011aligned, and inspiring\u2014reflecting national innovation goals\u2014I drafted a non\u2011technical rewrite.\\n\\nWhat I did:\\n- Opened the project at http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands and reviewed the current README.\\n- Consulted Fatima for tone and messaging priorities.\\n- Created a stakeholder\u2011friendly rewrite focused on vision, value, trust, and easy onboarding.\\n\\nDeliverable:\\n- Saved the 